WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.158 --> 00:00:04.036
-The prosecutor
in a criminal investigation

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.605
of Donald Trump's
business dealings

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:08.641
has convened a grand jury
that could decide

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.377
whether to indict Trump or
executives at his company.

00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:14.046
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:17.516
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:19.886
For the four years
of Trump's presidency,

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.620
we kept hearing
about the possibility

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.456
that Trump could maybe
potentially,

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:27.560
hypothetically face some
eventual legal consequences.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.862
There was the Mueller Report,
two impeachments,

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:31.231
the Michael Cohen case,

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.000
where he was essentially
an unindicted coconspirator.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.004
Every news story for four years
had a thin veneer of crime.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.305
You wouldn't have been
surprised to see

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.407
a lower third on CNN that read,

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:42.975
"Trump meets
with Polish President,

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.844
who claims
his wallet is missing."

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.346
Or how about
the emoluments clause?

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.147
Remember that --
when we all had to learn

00:00:48.147 --> 00:00:50.483
what an emolument was --
a completely useless

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.152
piece of information we all
had to store in our brains,

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:54.754
because the framers'
worst nightmare,

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.656
a shady real-estate grifter

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.391
with business dealings
in foreign countries,

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.359
accidentally became president?

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.794
If you asked Benjamin Franklin,

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.496
"Is it cool if
a bunch of Saudi lobbyists

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:06.732
stay at the president's hotel
to curry favor with him?"

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:08.534
he'd be so shocked,
he'd probably

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.737
fall off his French prostitute.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.939
So, we wasted all that time
learning about emoluments,

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.074
only for the Supreme Court to
dismiss the case against Trump

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.776
after he left office.
They basically said,

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.279
"Yeah, we, uh -- we stopped
prosecuting for that."

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.580
You know, it's like
when you go to Subway

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.915
and demand a $5 Footlong,
only for them to say,

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:25.117
"We don't do that anymore."
So you say, "Well,

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.052
has anything else around here
changed I should know about?"

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.088
And then they whisper,
"Have you heard about Jared?"

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.957
And you say, "No!",
even though you have heard,

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:33.793
because you still want to
hear them tell it.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.496
The point is, Trump has been
in potential legal hot water

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.864
for a while now,
as evidenced not just by

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:41.934
his own criminal probe
but all the criminals,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.503
or alleged criminals,
surrounding him.

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:46.439
-The immediate past President
of the United States

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.174
had to pardon
his campaign manager,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.142
had to pardon his longest-
standing political adviser,

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.945
had to pardon his
national security adviser,

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.779
had to pardon
his foreign policy adviser,

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:56.048
had to pardon the deputy chair
of his inaugural,

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.217
and his deputy campaign chairman
went to prison,

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.686
and his personal lawyer
went to prison,

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.220
and his other personal lawyer is

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.955
under federal
criminal investigation,

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.691
and he himself personally
is named by prosecutors

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:09.294
as an unindicted coconspirator
in multiple federal felonies.

00:02:09.294 --> 00:02:12.865
And he himself personally is
currently, as we speak,

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:16.269
under active criminal
investigation in two states.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.438
-it's just basic logic
that if you're surrounded

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.072
at all times
by that many criminals,

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:23.142
there's a solid chance
you're also a criminal.

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:25.611
You never hear someone
onstage at a concert say,

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.980
"That's Doug on the bass;
give it up for Russell

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.516
on rhythm guitar;
that's Mick on lead;

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:31.751
that's Billy on keyboards;

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.754
and me, oh, I'm not in a band.
I don't do music.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:36.356
Those guys do. Not me."

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.958
But we're
in an unprecedented situation,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.661
where the previous president
is under at least two

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.163
criminal investigations
in two different states,

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.632
one of which has now reached
the grand-jury stage.

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:48.234
If Obama
were under investigation,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.968
we'd be talking about that, too,
but he's not.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.972
The only news Obama makes
these days is showbiz-related.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.808
In fact, if you hear
about Obama investigations,

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.211
it's probably a new show
on HBO Max.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:01.214
Fingers crossed, it doesn't
take place in Philly, too.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.549
"Now, I'm gonna tell you
who the killer is.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:07.086
But, first, I need
a glass of, uh, 'wooder.'"

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.821
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.324
As for Trump, the only news
he makes today is

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.992
what he issues
in an official statement,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:16.062
calling a horse a junkie,
or when one of

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.764
the criminal investigations
on him takes a big step.

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.332
And that's what we learned
last night.

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:22.769
-We've got breaking news
in a criminal probe

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.003
into the Trump Organization.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.405
"The Washington Post"
just breaking the news

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:28.273
that the Manhattan
district attorney

00:03:28.273 --> 00:03:29.942
has convened a grand jury

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.311
that could weigh
potential criminal charges

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.914
against former President Trump
and his associates.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.916
From that "Washington Post"
report,

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:40.119
the move indicates that
district attorney Cyrus Vance's

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.222
investigation of the former
President and his business

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:46.492
has reached an advanced stage,
after more than two years.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.361
It suggests, too,
that Vance believes

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.162
he has found
evidence of a crime,

00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:52.765
if not by Trump, then
by someone potentially close

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.700
to him
or by his company.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.836
-I mean, I'm just shocked
it took two years.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:59.939
Trump has arguably confessed
to multiple crimes in public,

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.909
incited a violent insurrection,
been impeached twice,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.978
was an unindicted coconspirator
in a hush-money case,

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:09.615
paid just $750
in federal Income taxes

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:12.952
while he was president,
and did everything possible

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.954
to hide his taxes
from public view.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.656
At this point, I wouldn't be
shocked if it turned out

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.925
he tried to claim a deduction
for a bribe.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:21.127
I mean, what else do we need,
Trump to show up

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:22.595
to a Fox interview
with a shovel

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.730
and a shirt that says,
"I love burying bodies"?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.799
But, of course, Trump
is the last guy

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.500
you'd want to trust
burying a body.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.002
Based on this video,
you'd be lucky

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.504
if he covered part of one hand.

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:33.973
"Did you fully cover him,
Donny?"

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.108
"I mean, I think
I got it pretty good.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:39.846
I mean, I'd be a little worried
if they had dogs."

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:42.381
So, there's a grand jury now.
That's news.

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.383
But, again,
I'm not getting my hopes up.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:45.585
Remember how many times
we thought

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.152
Trump was on the verge
of going down?

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:48.988
Remember how everybody
at your gym

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.257
was working out
in "Mueller Time" T-shirt,

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.258
and now Goodwill
won't even take them?

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:55.194
Trump always manages
to wriggle out of a jam.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.262
He's like
the David Blaine of crime.

00:04:57.262 --> 00:05:00.433
If he ever goes to trial,
he'll just regurgitate a frog

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.468
that has "not guilty"
written on its back.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.803
If the feds come for him,
he'll hide out

00:05:04.803 --> 00:05:06.872
in a glass box over the Thames.

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:09.274
That said, we do know
that even before

00:05:09.274 --> 00:05:11.043
this latest news,
there have been

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:12.912
some pretty serious developments
in this case.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:14.613
The Manhattan D.A.
got Trump's taxes,

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:15.982
the New York state
attorney general

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:18.450
joined the criminal case,
and prosecutors met

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.186
with Trump's former fixer,
Michael Cohen,

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:22.154
at least eight times.
I mean, I bet

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.623
they got everything they needed
the first time

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:26.091
and then just kept bringing him
back for the zingers.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:28.728
-I think Donald Trump is gonna
flip on all of them.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:31.364
What do you think about that?
Including his children.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.099
So he's gonna
turn on his accountant

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.467
and point the finger.
He's gonna say,

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:37.403
"Don Jr. Handled that,
Ivanka handled that.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.905
Melania --
Don't take me, take Melania."

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:42.408
-Man, Michael Cohen is just
a totally different guy now.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.443
Loose, confident,
laughing it up, having fun.

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:47.179
He used to be the terrifying
mob-style bag man,

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:49.681
and now he's coming off
like a shipwrecked Ray Romano.

00:05:49.681 --> 00:05:51.651
"Oh, I don't know,
Trump would say,

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:54.286
I don't know,
'Ah, fix this for me.'

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:58.257
I-I-I can't.
You know, I got a tee time.

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.726
[ Laughter ]
"Raymond."

00:06:00.726 --> 00:06:02.728
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:05.330
Oh, you can't write the
Brad Garrett impression in,

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.265
Dave.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.265 --> 00:06:09.068
I also totally believe

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.969
that Trump would throw
his family under the bus.

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:13.205
You think he named
his eldest son after himself

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:15.675
for sentimental reasons?
He did it so there'd be

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:17.810
a second Donald Trump
to pin the blame on.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.011
"He's the one you want.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.579
That's why he's
hiding out in the woods."

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.348
I mean, look at that.
They caught him

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.417
because he waited
for someone else to come

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.885
and build him a Unabomber cabin.

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:29.755
And I have no trouble believing
he'd flip on Melania, too.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:33.125
"Mel! Mel, the feds are here.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:36.061
They want to know why you
committed all that tax fraud.

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:37.697
She'll be right down.
Just give her a second.

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:40.599
Mel, why are you
flushing the toilet?

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:42.267
Is it evidence, Mel?

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.804
I know you don't go potty
when people are in the house.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:47.306
She loves destroying evidence.
That's a serious charge, too.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.507
She's gonna go away
for a while, huh?

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:50.610
I'm gonna miss her.
Mel?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.678
I hope --
Those are big handcuffs.

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.113
They're gonna come right off
her lady wrists.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:55.648
Oh, no, are those for me?"

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.516
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:59.785
But Cohen is actually
a key figure here,

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:02.521
because, as you may recall,
he testified to Congress

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:05.291
that Trump had lied about
the value of his properties

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:07.192
for tax or insurance purposes.

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:09.829
Cohen even named specific people
in the Trump Organization

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.464
with knowledge of
Trump's practices.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.032
-To your knowledge,
did the president ever

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:16.135
provide inflated assets
to an insurance company?

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.870
-Yes.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.739
-Who else knows that
the president did this?

00:07:20.739 --> 00:07:23.809
-Allen Weisselberg,
Ron Lieberman,

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:25.411
and Matthew Calamari.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.512
-Remember that, you guys,
when we all found out

00:07:27.512 --> 00:07:30.048
about the existence of a guy
named Matthew Calamari?

00:07:30.048 --> 00:07:32.818
A name that sounds like
a Super Mario rip-off

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:34.653
your grandma would buy
at the dollar store?

00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:36.656
That's his actual name.
When I first heard it,

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:37.923
I thought it was
a Mafia nickname,

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:39.692
like "Paulie Walnuts."
"This is a guy,

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:42.228
Matthew D'Angelo,
AKA Matthew Calamari."

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:44.129
Sounds like a character
that got cut

00:07:44.129 --> 00:07:45.264
from the "SpongeBob" musical.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.633
I have no idea
who Matthew Calamari is,

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.635
but based on his name alone,
I can tell the feds

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:52.804
exactly where to find him --
slipping $6 in singles

00:07:52.804 --> 00:07:54.640
to the maître d' at Del Frisco's

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.675
to get a table
by the air-conditioner.

00:07:56.675 --> 00:07:59.645
"Hey, let's not have fried
Calamari tonight, alright?"

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:02.114
The other guy
Cohen mentioned there is

00:08:02.114 --> 00:08:04.049
Trump's money man,
Allen Weisselberg,

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:06.252
the chief financial officer
of the Trump Organization.

00:08:06.252 --> 00:08:08.587
The prosecutors are apparently
focused on Weisselberg.

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:11.257
And when asked if he would
potentially flip on Trump,

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:13.859
Weisselberg's
ex-daughter-in-law, who has said

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.928
she's also cooperated
with the investigation,

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:17.262
did not hesitate.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:19.632
-One person now cooperating
with the investigations

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:21.600
into Weisselberg
and the Trump Organization

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.934
is on your screen there --

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:25.605
Allen Weisselberg's former
daughter-in-law, Jennifer,

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:27.607
who was married
to Weisselberg's son Barry

00:08:27.607 --> 00:08:31.177
for 14 years,
until their divorce in 2018.

00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:33.445
Jennifer Weisselberg's lawyer
says she has

00:08:33.445 --> 00:08:35.214
25 years of financial records,

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:37.083
some of which
have been subpoenaed.

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:39.151
Will Allen Weisselberg
flip on Trump?

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.555
-Yes.

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:45.690
-wow,

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.160
I mean, no hesitation at all
with your answer there.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.461
-No hesitation at all?

00:08:49.461 --> 00:08:50.463
I'm guessing,
when you work for Trump,

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:51.797
you start thinking
about flipping

00:08:51.797 --> 00:08:53.232
as soon as you get the gig.
It's like when you're

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.501
in the middle of a job interview
at Little Caesars

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:57.903
and you're already fantasizing
about how you're gonna quit.

00:08:57.903 --> 00:09:00.139
"You can take this job
and shove it, shove it."

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:03.376
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:05.044
"Trump's inner circle flips

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:08.080
more than the short-order cook
at IHOP."

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.216
Hey, here's the thing, guys.

00:09:11.216 --> 00:09:13.752
You want to take away
my Vince Vaughn,

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:15.521
you're gonna get
a little Dennis Miller

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:18.023
and a little Ray Romano.
That's the trade-off.

00:09:18.023 --> 00:09:20.025
I'm not gonna just
stop with the impressions,

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:24.063
because -- guess what? --
I don't like my voice that much.

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.898
[ Laughter ]

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.600
Cohen went on to explain
that Trump...

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.134
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:30.903
Cohen went on to explain
that Trump deflated

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:33.939
the value of his assets in order
to avoid paying taxes on them.

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:35.774
-To your knowledge,
was the president interested

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:38.744
in reducing his local
real-estate bills -- tax bills?

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:41.146
-Yes.
-And how did he do that?

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:44.516
-What you do is you deflate
the value of the asset,

00:09:44.516 --> 00:09:48.187
and then you put in a request
to the tax department

00:09:48.187 --> 00:09:50.623
for a deduction.

00:09:50.623 --> 00:09:53.058
-"Trump's assets
are more deflated

00:09:53.058 --> 00:09:55.861
than a lawn Santa
on January 10th."

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:58.263
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.263 --> 00:10:00.966
"Raymond, I don't get it."
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:03.969
There's a good chance
that Cohen's testimony was

00:10:03.969 --> 00:10:07.106
the first time Trump heard
that scheme explained

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:10.009
in such specific detail.
"That's how you do it?

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:11.911
Oh, well,
that sounds very illegal."

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:13.279
And according
to "The Washington Post,"

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.214
that's precisely
one of the things

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:16.681
prosecutors are looking into.

00:10:16.681 --> 00:10:18.550
-His investigators
are scrutinizing

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:21.286
Trump's business practices
before he was president,

00:10:21.286 --> 00:10:23.889
including whether the value
of specific properties

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:26.558
in the Trump Organization's
real-estate portfolio

00:10:26.558 --> 00:10:28.126
were manipulated in a way

00:10:28.126 --> 00:10:30.362
that defrauded banks and
insurance companies

00:10:30.362 --> 00:10:32.965
and if any tax benefits
were obtained illegally

00:10:32.965 --> 00:10:35.967
through unscrupulous
asset valuation.

00:10:35.967 --> 00:10:37.836
-In addition to being
a potential crime,

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:40.372
unscrupulous asset valuation
sounds like

00:10:40.372 --> 00:10:43.175
something Trump would put under
"interests" on his Tinder bio.

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.678
You know, one thing I've
always thought was so funny

00:10:45.678 --> 00:10:47.113
about Trump's legal troubles is,

00:10:47.113 --> 00:10:49.248
that if Trump
hadn't run for president,

00:10:49.248 --> 00:10:53.151
he probably would have gotten
away with all of this stuff --

00:10:53.151 --> 00:10:55.888
defrauding banks,
deflating assets.

00:10:55.888 --> 00:10:58.423
Rich people get away
with that stuff all the time.

00:10:58.423 --> 00:11:01.493
And the banks just shrug
and raise our ATM fees.

00:11:01.493 --> 00:11:03.595
No one cared
about Trump's tax returns

00:11:03.595 --> 00:11:05.097
when he was just
a cable news blowhard

00:11:05.097 --> 00:11:06.965
who called in to "Fox &amp; Friends"
to shoot the [Bleep]

00:11:06.965 --> 00:11:08.901
or spent his time tweeting
about Diet Coke.

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:11.837
But Trump had to go and run
for president like a moron

00:11:11.837 --> 00:11:14.006
and attract the attention
of prosecutors

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:16.742
scrutinizing every aspect
of his life and business,

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:18.177
which is not a good idea

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:20.045
when you're famously
a corrupt real-estate mogul

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:22.514
and reality-show host,
surrounded by shady characters.

00:11:22.514 --> 00:11:24.482
Like, I don't want to
make any assumptions,

00:11:24.482 --> 00:11:26.718
but if Mystery the pickup artist
ran for president,

00:11:26.718 --> 00:11:28.186
I'm pretty sure they'd find
some weird stuff

00:11:28.186 --> 00:11:29.388
in his tax returns, too.

00:11:29.388 --> 00:11:31.189
Hey, mystery, under "Income,"
it just says,

00:11:31.189 --> 00:11:33.091
"Women love
the scent of confidence."

00:11:33.091 --> 00:11:34.226
What does that mean?

00:11:34.226 --> 00:11:36.027
"It means Venus is
the goddess of love."

00:11:36.027 --> 00:11:38.831
Okay, and under "Assets,"
all you have listed are

00:11:38.831 --> 00:11:40.899
a bunch of puka shell necklaces?

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:43.069
"And?"
[ Laughter ]

00:11:43.069 --> 00:11:45.871
This is
an unprecedented situation.

00:11:45.871 --> 00:11:48.807
Virtually the entirety of one of
our two political parties

00:11:48.807 --> 00:11:51.009
has devoted itself
to a corrupt ex-president

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:52.377
who is currently under

00:11:52.377 --> 00:11:54.313
an intensifying
criminal investigation

00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:56.182
which has now reached
the grand-jury stage.

00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:58.851
Trump is talking about running
for president again in 2024,

00:11:58.851 --> 00:12:01.586
but if he's in jail,
he might have to tell the GOP...

00:12:01.586 --> 00:12:03.455
-"Don't take me, take Melania."

00:12:03.455 --> 00:12:05.390
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:09.161
[ Theme music plays ]

